@participant6 

In your scheduler, can you also somehow debug whether the number of elements in `inFlightPods` and `inFlightEvents` are/is growing along with the memory consumption, by adding some logs etc in addition to the patch https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/126962?
https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/release-1.31/pkg/scheduler/internal/queue/scheduling_queue.go#L185-L211

For example, just like this:

```go
func (p *PriorityQueue) Pop(logger klog.Logger) (*framework.QueuedPodInfo, error) {
//...
	logger.Info("DEBUG: the number of inflight pods/events", "inFlightPods", len(p.inFlightPods), "inFlightEvents", p.inFlightEvents.Len())
}
```

Here, I'd like to make sure either of inFlightPods or inFlightEvents is the root cause.
